{
  "id": "COMPOUND:980 - PROTEIN:5232",
  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is linked to MPP-89 through a series of molecular interactions involving purinoceptors and a compound known as [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate. This compound is both a target of doxorubicin and a target of palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets MPP-89. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act through a pathway where it first binds to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is then targeted by a secondary compound, leading to the activation of MPP-89. The shared involvement of this compound in multiple pathways supports a potential mechanism where doxorubicin indirectly influences MPP-89 via a purinoceptor-mediated route. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on purinoceptor signaling, which may be a key mechanism underlying the interaction between doxorubicin and MPP-89.",
